// One free function per struct that has something to free below its own block
// (docs/MEMORY.md 3.5b): `idfr_NAME(p)` hands the struct to the runtime's
// work-stack drain id_frs_run with the struct's own step `idfs_NAME` (step.id),
// which frees by the field types with no descriptor read at run time. The
// analysis names idfr_NAME (esc_dfn) wherever a deep-owned struct is given
// back, so a wrapper exists for exactly the structs it can ask for. The steps
// are declared first because a struct's step names the steps of the structs
// below it. The descriptor walk (id_free_walk) stays in the runtime for the
// LLVM target, which still emits its wrappers from esc_desc.

emit_frees() {
  emit_free_protos();
  int i = 0;
  while(i < len((import sdname))) {
    emit_free_one((import sdname)[i]);
    i = i + 1;
  }
} return void;
